cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "wildphylo: a config-driven phylodynamics pipeline for wildlife disease"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, config-driven pipeline for phylodynamic analysis of wildlife
  pathogens from public sequence data. Covers curation, alignment QC, ML
  phylogeny, automated temporal-signal assessment, stratified subsampling,
  Bayesian inference with discrete trait reconstruction, segment congruence
  screening for segmented genomes, and Nextstrain builds with scheduled
  rebuilds.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nightingale
    given-names: Batya
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0706-8951"
# Drafted in collaboration with Claude (Anthropic); see the Acknowledgements
# section of README.md. Not listed as an author, because authorship entails
# accountability that a model cannot hold.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/batyanight/wildphylo"
keywords:
  - phylodynamics
  - wildlife disease
  - molecular epidemiology
  - BEAST
  - Nextstrain
  - reproducibility
